    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. The main issue is that the neighbor's fence actually encroaches about three feet into our property line, which is creating a headache with the setback calculations for the new MU building. Since the code is vague on whether an existing encroachment can be \"grandfathered\" or if it invalidates the setback compliance for a reclassification, do you think we should focus our argument on the \"non-conforming use\" angle, or is it better to just prepare for a variance request?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
