      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Given the pre-existing encroachment, focusing on the \"non-conforming use\" angle might be challenging since you are seeking a *change* in zoning, not just differing from existing rules. Preparing for a variance request, specifically one tied to the proven existing encroachment, is likely the more direct path forward. In your variance application, you must demonstrate how the encroachment is not detrimental and that the variance is necessary for a reasonable use of the property.",
